1
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,640
 I'll be there in a jiffy, Peter.

2
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:28,550
 The human body gets energy in the nicest way from delicious meals like this.

3
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:31,480
 But a meal is only raw material.

4
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:40,410
 The body has to extract the energy from the foodstuffs by digesting them.

5
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:47,280
 To our food, it is the first step in the long process of digestion, a process which transforms

6
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:59,050
 matter into energy.

7
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:05,230
 The food is about to travel down the oesophagus, the tube that leads to the stomach.

8
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:12,210
 Meanwhile, in the nucleus of a nearby nerve cell...

9
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:17,110
 Chief! The message is on its way!

10
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:22,280
 Lot are asleep on your feet. Can't you see that some food is on its way down already?

11
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:26,830
 Send out an immediate order to the muscles in the wall of the esophagus. Let's get them moving!

12
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:31,480
 Immediate orders for the muscles in the wall of the esophagus!

13
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:51,160
 And you lazy luts go down to some work, isn't it?

14
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:55,010
 Come on, you loafers. I need you wide awake for this.

15
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:55,960
 Now!

16
00:01:55,960 --> 00:02:35,420
 Two, one, two, one, two, one, two, one, two, one, two, one, two, one, two...

17
00:02:35,420 --> 00:03:09,120
 15,5 kilojoules starch.

18
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,600
 Well, there's some sugar, plenty of it too.

19
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:18,130
 More fat, a few units of vitamin D, that's good.

20
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:23,430
 You can let that lot through, it's fine, but there's no need to rush.

21
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:27,570
 We don't want a blockage, it's bad enough the way these children broke their food.

22
00:03:27,990 --> 00:03:29,310
 Clear the way to the stomach.

23
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:15,530
 Gastric juices is like a processing factory,

24
00:04:15,970 --> 00:04:20,050
 where all the jumbled elements of the food are separated and classified.

25
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:27,480
 Fiber, minerals, vitamins, starches, sugars, proteins.

26
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:33,470
 All the ingredients of Jumbo's lunch are broken down and dissolved in the gastric juices

27
00:04:33,470 --> 00:04:47,340
 The food is arriving. When digestion begins, we're going to need a lot more juice

28
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:50,740
 We'd better increase the rate of flow immediately

29
00:04:50,740 --> 00:05:01,220
 We're going to need all the gastric enzymes, I think

30
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:06,210
 Calling all gastric enzymes, calling all gastric enzymes, report for duty immediately

31
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:21,320
 They're off to the stomach, my child, in the very devil of a hurry because they're needed

32
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,700
 When duty calls, those enzymes drop everything and scramble

33
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:28,320
 Let them get on with their digestion by all means

34
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,270
 but they could show us some consideration.

35
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,850
 Our oxygen is precious!

36
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:33,850
 It's an imported commodity after all.

37
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:39,160
 Hormones, small but fast-acting.

38
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:41,660
 Their calling in life is to trigger the gastric enzymes

39
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:43,100
 along when they need it.

40
00:05:43,100 --> 00:06:38,460
 Look over there.

41
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:52,350
 Working enzymes take a break from their digestive tasks,

42
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:55,360
 but it's not long before they're inundated again

43
00:06:55,360 --> 00:07:03,880
 to get on top of their workload at last.

44
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,880
 Peptides, amino acids, and coagulated milk.

45
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,380
 It all seems to be in order.

46
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:10,940
 And far too much sugar, as usual.

47
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:22,130
 Look at all the fat he's asking for indigestion.

48
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:25,130
 Open the pyloric sphincter and clear the way to the small intestine.

49
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:43,700
 Where do you think you're going?

50
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:44,700
 Oh, us, officer.

51
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:47,050
 We're E. coli bacteria.

52
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,960
 We live in the small intestine, officer.

53
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:51,300
 Yes, officer, it's down in that direction.

54
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:54,300
 But I think we'd best be getting along now, so goodbye.

55
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:58,880
 They claim to be E. coli bacteria, but they remind me of salmonella.

56
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:00,030
 Wait!

57
00:08:00,030 --> 00:08:01,090
 You bacteria!

58
00:08:01,090 --> 00:08:05,330
 Come back here, I want to see your papers.

59
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:14,100
 have swore. Jumbo, you're getting stuck into that apple pie, alright? It's so delicious, Peter. I'll

60
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:19,230
 just have another tiny helping. But you've had enough already. I'm a growing boy with a healthy

61
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:51,520
 appetite. Mmm. It's all the sugar. It's disgusting. Priority message for the gallbladder. Step up

62
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:56,920
 production of bile immediately or we'll never manage to digest all this extra fat. You'd better

63
00:08:56,920 --> 00:09:00,880
 let the pancreas know that we need more enzymes and plenty of them to deal with all that sugar.

64
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:33,560
 Ka-cha. Even if the stomach did a great part of the work, we'd be lost without that bile from the

65
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:37,470
 liver to digest fats for us?

66
00:09:37,470 --> 00:09:39,660
 Pancreatic enzymes I ordered.

67
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,660
 We need them to deal with the sugar and protein.

68
00:09:41,660 --> 00:10:03,350
 Bacteri...

69
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:07,700
 Come down, you silly boy. Those e-coly bacteria are on our side.

70
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,760
 You didn't learn very much at school, did you?

71
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:19,090
 You'll see a few million more of those before the day is over.

72
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:20,110
 Cellulose.

73
00:10:20,110 --> 00:10:24,590
 Yes, Emmeline, my dear. The skin of an apple is tailor-made for us, isn't it?

74
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:30,840
 You girls are knitting vitamins again.

75
00:10:30,840 --> 00:11:00,230
 And where would the body be without the vitamins we so obliged to be manufacturer? Answer me that.

76
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:05,160
 It's a brain. It's just what he wants to.

77
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,950
 Yes, and it's mostly between mealtimes, isn't it?

78
00:11:08,010 --> 00:11:09,390
 Come on, Enz, I'll talk to it.

79
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:30,740
 That awful rumble.

80
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:33,540
 Your attention, please. The stomach is overloaded.

81
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:36,180
 Emergency evacuation of contents is imminent.

82
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:39,390
 What does he mean by that, Chief? Evacuation of contents?

83
00:11:40,110 --> 00:11:42,170
 Going to throw up.

84
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:43,730
 Shall we tune in, then?

85
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:44,860
 By all means.

86
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:56,930
 Stop it, you glutton. Stop it.

87
00:11:57,490 --> 00:11:59,590
 That really is the last talk.

88
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:17,210
 Better in a couple of minutes.

89
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:19,680
 Here, drink this, my child. It should help you.

90
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:31,400
 It's working. He's a lucky boy.

91
00:12:32,110 --> 00:12:34,810
 That's what happens when you gorge on rich food, understand?

92
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:37,390
 Mind you, Jumbo deserves some sympathy.

93
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:38,670
 That pie was delicious.

94
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:41,270
 Well, that's that.

95
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:43,810
 Now, let's get on with the digestive process.

96
00:12:44,050 --> 00:12:44,570
 Where were we?

97
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:48,090
 Of course, here in the duodenum.

98
00:12:48,890 --> 00:12:50,390
 Circulation seems to be okay.

99
00:12:56,330 --> 00:13:02,510
 Lucky he is to have a young, strong liver

100
00:13:02,510 --> 00:13:05,450
 that works so hard at getting rid of undesirable substances.

101
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:08,450
 But I'll tell you about the liver some other time.

102
00:13:08,450 --> 00:13:10,510
 The liver is miraculous.

103
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,920
 The pancreas is a fascinating organ, too.

104
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:18,510
 Here we go.

105
00:13:19,330 --> 00:13:22,870
 Quiet, isn't it, Moistro?

106
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,180
 Yes, thank goodness.

107
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,940
 Good morning to the pair of you.

108
00:13:26,270 --> 00:13:27,250
 No complaints, then?

109
00:13:27,370 --> 00:13:27,970
 The usual.

110
00:13:28,270 --> 00:13:29,470
 Nothing to write home about.

111
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:33,020
 Mind you, a quick squeeze down the small intestine wouldn't go amiss.

112
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:37,380
 Poor Jumbo's been sick already today, and we don't want him getting diarrhoea into the bargain.

113
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:38,570
 Good idea.

114
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,400
 Right, let's get back to work.

115
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,660
 I want to take a much closer look at the villi in the small intestine.

116
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:55,040
 The intestine is carpeted with tentacle-like villi, which have very thin walls and a very rich blood supply.

117
00:13:55,570 --> 00:13:59,310
 This is where they all leave the digestive system and into the bloodstream

118
00:13:59,310 --> 00:14:01,670
 by squeezing through the walls of the blood vessels.

119
00:14:02,010 --> 00:14:03,890
 Sugars, salts, fats, vitamins.

120
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:20,340
 Sorry, but you amino acids aren't allowed to hitchhike.

121
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:24,260
 You're supposed to find your own way to the liver up the hepatic portal vessel.

122
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:26,890
 Can't miss it if you go straight along there.

123
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:31,970
 You can't get on, fatty, and they'll have to get off again.

124
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,810
 Fats go via the lymphatic system, as if you didn't know.

125
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:48,500
 Oxide, Hemo?

126
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:49,910
 Never mind, Hemo.

127
00:14:50,090 --> 00:14:53,230
 When you pass through the liver, you'll come out feeling clean and refreshed.

128
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:58,650
 Get your heads down.

129
00:15:03,330 --> 00:15:06,020
 Look at that, Captain.

130
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:08,160
 Salmonella bacteria.

131
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:10,560
 They're the ones who cause food poisoning.

132
00:15:11,430 --> 00:15:12,990
 Calling all antibody units.

133
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:13,700
 Urgent!

134
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:17,240
 Reporting the presence of Salmonella in the small intestine.

135
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,940
 They are located in the duodenum.

136
00:15:20,310 --> 00:15:21,890
 Send the anti-Salmonella squad.

137
00:15:22,210 --> 00:15:24,810
 We're also going to need some extra macrophage support.

138
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:40,280
 Come on, let's get out of here.

139
00:15:47,790 --> 00:15:55,600
 Fish, Captain.

140
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:56,280
 Hold it, Lieutenant.

141
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:57,970
 I think the colonel's coming through.

142
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:00,260
 Situation under control, Colonel.

143
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:03,400
 A few Salmonella successfully infiltrated the small intestine,

144
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,440
 And our macrophages made short work of them.

145
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:05,740
 Good.

146
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:07,920
 Thank you, sir.

147
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:19,160
 Jumbo seems recovered from his nausea and from the salmonella,

148
00:16:19,510 --> 00:16:23,460
 which entered his system because he didn't wash his hands before eating.

149
00:16:24,110 --> 00:16:28,400
 And now his inside calmly continues with the process of digestion.

150
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:32,380
 Rush hour is over,

151
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:37,630
 but various bacteria lie in wait ready to mop up struggling dietary fibers.

152
00:16:38,650 --> 00:16:39,970
 Mr. Policeman, Mr. Policeman,

153
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:42,080
 those nasty bacteria won't leave us alone.

154
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:45,500
 We do a worthwhile job too, you know, we clear up.

155
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:56,700
 Polybacterium busy splitting proteids up into amino acids.

156
00:16:56,700 --> 00:17:00,510
 One of her colleagues is sniffing round to see what she can find.

157
00:17:00,510 --> 00:17:03,680
 While others are busy making vitamins.

158
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:08,040
 Girls, don't forget the vitamin B, my dears, will you now?

159
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:10,440
 It'll be needed for making new blood, won't it?

160
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,980
 And what about K?

161
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:14,520
 The blood won't clot without it.

162
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:16,620
 I can never remember the pattern for B.

163
00:17:16,620 --> 00:17:18,370
 Give it here and I'll show you.

164
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:28,550
 Fibre seems to be the only surviving remnant of Jumbo's delicious lunch.

165
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:32,830
 Now we pass into the large intestine, where the fibres are handled quite roughly.

166
00:17:32,830 --> 00:17:44,350
 The freezing removes the moisture from the fibres.

167
00:17:44,950 --> 00:17:50,350
 It is absorbed through the walls of the intestine, while the fibres go marching on.

168
00:18:00,470 --> 00:18:04,380
 That's the appendix, dear.

169
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,540
 Well, what's it for?

170
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:09,140
 Absolutely nothing apart from getting appendicitis.

171
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:18,820
 Gee, as we come to the tail end of the digestive process,

172
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:23,180
 there are punishment, friendly bacteria, and antibodies, all on their guard.

173
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,870
 But why do we need so many of them, chief?

174
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:28,130
 Well, this is the end of the digestive process.

175
00:18:28,470 --> 00:18:31,510
 And just supposing a few harmful germs had got this far,

176
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:33,830
 it would be an ideal place for them to multiply.

177
00:18:34,010 --> 00:18:35,310
 The climate is perfect for them.

178
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:40,480
 There are thousands of friendly bacteria out there who help us with digestion.

179
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,260
 They give their services free.

180
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:42,740
 Oh!

181
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,660
 Right, now let's get down to some work.

182
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,690
 Okay, you guys, this is it.

183
00:18:47,890 --> 00:18:49,750
 Wait for my signal, then start multiplying.

184
00:18:49,870 --> 00:18:51,190
 We'll catch them napping.

185
00:18:51,550 --> 00:18:52,150
 Ha ha ha ha!

186
00:18:52,330 --> 00:18:52,740
 Ready?

187
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:55,060
 Divide!

188
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:09,470
 Why don't you answer?

189
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:13,730
 Wonderful, you're the sooner the better.

190
00:19:13,730 --> 00:19:25,570
 This is an alert.

191
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,940
 There's a large salmonella presence in the colon.

192
00:19:28,410 --> 00:19:29,280
 Come in, police.

193
00:19:29,850 --> 00:19:31,860
 All patrolmen must report immediately.

194
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:39,780
 Antibodies.

195
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:46,990
 There's an emergency.

196
00:19:47,710 --> 00:19:49,150
 Their members are increasing by the minute.

197
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:54,430
 We desperately need a squad of highly trained and dedicated fighters equipped to deal with salmonella.

198
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:57,560
 We've got them, you guys.

199
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:01,190
 In the meantime, just keep on multiplying.

200
00:20:02,390 --> 00:20:06,720
 We're going to reduce this child's digestive tract to him.

201
00:20:09,090 --> 00:20:15,740
 Sleep so soundly if he knew that an army of germs was planning to take over his body.

202
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:19,860
 If they succeed, it's his own fault for not washing his hands.

203
00:20:25,230 --> 00:20:34,820
 His engagement promises to be a major battle and Colonel Peter is in overall command.

204
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:36,630
 They're multiplying even more rapidly.

205
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:38,040
 We must attack now.

206
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:40,350
 Metro, here are your orders.

207
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:44,040
 Attack the enemy's left flank with your special antibody squad.

208
00:20:44,490 --> 00:20:48,250
 Lieutenant Jumbo Jr. will hit them hard in the center with his polynuclear brigade.

209
00:20:48,430 --> 00:20:49,250
 Take no prisoners.

210
00:20:49,530 --> 00:20:54,630
 Lieutenant Clare, I want you to cover our right flank with your lymphocyte units, understood?

211
00:20:54,970 --> 00:20:56,210
 Message received, Colonel.

212
00:20:56,970 --> 00:21:01,140
 Captain Peter, I'm delegating overall command of this entire operation to you.

213
00:21:01,370 --> 00:21:02,550
 I'll be counting on you.

214
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:04,530
 I won't let you down, Colonel.

215
00:21:40,430 --> 00:22:05,050
 Friendly bacteria.

216
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:10,400
 Me, your assistant urgently requested to help fight off a massive salmonella invasion.

217
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,440
 Please, come quickly.

218
00:22:11,650 --> 00:22:13,150
 Right you are then, sir.

219
00:22:22,420 --> 00:22:29,440
 I come at last.

220
00:22:30,270 --> 00:22:31,960
 There was no need to worry, Captain.

221
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:34,820
 You know that we e-colies would never leave you in the ledge.

222
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:37,360
 I know that, Chief, but there aren't very many of you, are there?

223
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:41,060
 We've got a few tricks up our sleeve, Captain, just you watch.

224
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:40,560
 ...tons of a human, millions of bacteria, all fighting for survival.

225
00:23:40,870 --> 00:23:43,330
 And some of them are very nasty characters indeed.

226
00:23:43,970 --> 00:23:48,540
 But the helpful bacteria tend to keep the bad ones in check.

227
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:53,260
 When the useful ones have got the upper hand, which is usually the case, then all's well.

228
00:23:53,630 --> 00:23:57,250
 The useful organisms win because they're in partnership with the body.

229
00:23:57,430 --> 00:23:59,360
 It shelters them and they protect it.

230
00:23:59,360 --> 00:24:02,920
 So our story of digestion is over.

231
00:24:03,550 --> 00:24:06,490
 And the last step is the elimination of waste products.

